#: ../../../xontrib.rst:5
msgid "Extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:8
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:9
msgid ""
"xonsh is an extensible, user-patchable platform: third-party developers can "
"build and distribute their own extensions without going through the xonsh "
"release cycle, and end users can reshape any subsystem directly from their :"
"doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` because every part of xonsh is a Python module. In "
"the xonsh ecosystem these extensions are called *xontribs*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:15
msgid "A xontrib can be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:17
msgid "a set of aliases — plain strings, lists, or callable Python functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:18
msgid "a tab-completer for a single command or a whole API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:19
msgid "a prompt field (e.g. battery, container, version-control, kubernetes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:20
msgid ""
"a handler for session events such as ``on_chdir``, ``on_postcommand``, or "
"``on_pre_prompt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:22
msgid "a new environment variable or ``$XONSH_*`` setting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:23
msgid ""
"a full subsystem — syntax-highlighting tokens, a history backend, an "
"integration with an external tool, and so on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:27
msgid "Search and Install Xontribs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:28
msgid "Two good places to look for xontribs published by the community:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:30
msgid ""
"`Awesome xontribs <https://xonsh.github.io/awesome-xontribs/>`_ — curated "
"list of xontribs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:32
msgid ""
"`GitHub xontrib topic <https://github.com/topics/xontrib>`_ — every "
"repository tagged with the ``xontrib`` topic on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:37
msgid "Listing Known Xontribs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:38
msgid ""
"The ``xontrib`` command allows you to list the installed xontribs. This "
"command will report if they are loaded in the current session. To display "
"this information, pass the ``list`` action to the ``xontrib`` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:42
msgid ""
"@ xontrib list\n"
"abbrevs             not-loaded          Expand command abbreviations while "
"typing in the Xonsh shell.\n"
"clp                 not-loaded          Copy output to clipboard. Cross-"
"platform.\n"
"cmd_done            not-loaded          Show long running commands durations "
"in prompt with option to send notification when terminal is not focused.\n"
"jedi                not-loaded          Use Jedi as xonsh's python "
"completer.\n"
"output_search       not-loaded          Get identifiers, paths, URLs and "
"words from the previous command output and use them for the next command in "
"xonsh shell\n"
"pipeliner           not-loaded          Let your pipe lines flow thru the "
"Python code in xonsh.\n"
"prompt_starship     not-loaded          Starship cross-shell prompt in xonsh "
"shell.\n"
"sh                  not-loaded          Paste and run commands from bash, "
"zsh, fish, tcsh in xonsh shell.\n"
"\n"
"@ xontrib info sh\n"
"Name: sh\n"
"Source: xontrib.sh at /Users/snail/.local/xonsh-env/lib/python3.14/site-"
"packages/xontrib/sh.py\n"
"Description: Paste and run commands from bash, zsh, fish, tcsh in xonsh "
"shell.\n"
"Loaded: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:60
msgid ""
"For programmatic access, you may also have this command print a JSON "
"formatted string:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:63
msgid ""
"@ $(@json xontrib list --json)['abbrevs']\n"
"{'name': 'abbrevs',\n"
" 'loaded': False,\n"
" 'auto': False,\n"
" 'module': 'xontrib.abbrevs',\n"
" 'description': 'Expand command abbreviations while typing in the Xonsh "
"shell.'}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:73
msgid "Loading Xontribs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:74
msgid ""
"Xontribs may be loaded in a few different ways: from your :doc:`xonsh RC "
"<xonshrc>`, dynamically at runtime with the ``xontrib`` command, or its "
"Python API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:77
msgid ""
"Extensions are loaded via the ``xontrib load`` command. This command may be "
"run from anywhere in your :doc:`xonsh RC <xonshrc>` or at any point after "
"xonsh has started up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:81
msgid "xontrib load myext mpl mypkg.show"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:85
msgid ""
"Pass ``-s`` (``--suppress-warnings``) to load every xontrib that is "
"installed and silently skip any name that isn't. Useful in a :doc:`xonsh RC "
"<xonshrc>` that is shared across machines where only a subset of xontribs is "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:89
msgid "The same can be done in Python as well"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:91
msgid ""
"from xonsh.xontribs import xontribs_load\n"
"xontribs_load(['myext', 'mpl', 'mypkg.show'])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:96
msgid ""
"A xontrib can be unloaded from the current session using ``xontrib unload``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:98
msgid "xontrib unload myext mpl mypkg.show"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:102
msgid ""
"Xontribs can use `setuptools entrypoints <https://setuptools.pypa.io/en/"
"latest/userguide/entry_point.html?highlight=entrypoints>`_ to mark "
"themselves available for autoloading using the below format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:105
msgid ""
"[options.entry_points]\n"
"xonsh.xontribs =\n"
"    xontrib_name = path.to.the.module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:111
msgid ""
"Here the module should contain ``_load_xontrib_`` function as described "
"above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:115
msgid ""
"Please make sure that importing the xontrib module and calling "
"``_load_xontrib_`` is fast enough. Otherwise it will affect the shell's "
"startup time. Any other imports or heavy computations should be done in lazy "
"manner whenever possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:121
msgid "Authoring Xontribs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:122
msgid ""
"The fastest way to start a new xontrib is the `xontrib-template <https://"
"github.com/xonsh/xontrib-template>`_ repository — a ready-to-publish "
"skeleton, packaging metadata, and the entry point pre-wired for autoloading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:127
msgid "Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:128
msgid ""
"Xontribs are modules with some special functions written in either xonsh "
"(``*.xsh``) or Python (``*.py``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:131
msgid "Here is a template:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:133
msgid ""
"from xonsh.built_ins import XonshSession\n"
"\n"
"def _load_xontrib_(xsh: XonshSession, **kwargs) -> dict:\n"
"    \"\"\"\n"
"    this function will be called when loading/reloading the xontrib.\n"
"\n"
"    Args:\n"
"        xsh: the current xonsh session instance, serves as the interface to "
"manipulate the session.\n"
"             This allows you to register new aliases, history backends, "
"event listeners ...\n"
"        **kwargs: it is empty as of now. Kept for future proofing.\n"
"    Returns:\n"
"        dict: this will get loaded into the current execution context\n"
"    \"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"def _unload_xontrib_(xsh: XonshSession, **kwargs) -> dict:\n"
"    \"\"\"If you want your extension to be unloadable, put that logic "
"here\"\"\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:154
msgid ""
"The xontrib must implement ``_unload_xontrib_`` itself. If this function is "
"not provided, any registered event handlers, environment variables, aliases, "
"and completers will remain active after ``xontribs unload/reload``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:158
msgid ""
"This _load_xontrib_() function is called after your extension is imported, "
"and the currently active :py:class:`xonsh.built_ins.XonshSession` instance "
"is passed as the argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:163
msgid ""
"Xontribs without ``_load_xontrib_`` are still supported. But when such "
"xontrib is loaded, variables listed in ``__all__`` are placed in the current "
"execution context if defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:168
msgid ""
"Normally, these are stored and found in an `implicit namespace package "
"<https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0420/>`_ called ``xontrib``. However, "
"xontribs may be placed in any package or directory that is on the "
"``$PYTHONPATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:173
msgid ""
"If a module is in the ``xontrib`` namespace package, it can be referred to "
"just by its module name. If a module is in any other package, then it must "
"be referred to by its full package path, separated by ``.`` like you would "
"in an import statement.  Of course, a module in ``xontrib`` may be referred "
"to with the full ``xontrib.myext``. But just calling it ``myext`` is a lot "
"shorter and one of the main advantages of placing an extension in the "
"``xontrib`` namespace package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:181
msgid ""
"Here is a sample file system layout and what the xontrib names would be::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:183
msgid ""
"|- xontrib/\n"
"   |- javert.xsh     # \"javert\", because in xontrib\n"
"   |- your.py        # \"your\",\n"
"   |- eyes/\n"
"      |- __init__.py\n"
"      |- scream.xsh  # \"eyes.scream\", because eyes is in xontrib\n"
"|- mypkg/\n"
"   |- __init__.py    # a regular package with an init file\n"
"   |- other.py       # not a xontrib\n"
"   |- show.py        # \"mypkg.show\", full module name\n"
"   |- tell.xsh       # \"mypkg.tell\", full module name\n"
"   |- subpkg/\n"
"      |- __init__.py\n"
"      |- done.py     # \"mypkg.subpkg.done\", full module name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:199
msgid ""
"You can also use the `xontrib template <https://github.com/xonsh/xontrib-"
"cookiecutter>`_ to easily create the layout for your xontrib package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:204
msgid "Tell Us About Your Xontrib!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:206
msgid ""
"To register a xontrib, create a ``PullRequest`` at `awesome-xontribs "
"<https://github.com/xonsh/awesome-xontribs>`_ repository. Also, if you use "
"Github to host your code, please add `xonsh <https://github.com/topics/"
"xonsh>`_ and `xontrib <https://github.com/topics/xontrib>`_ to the topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../xontrib.rst:212
msgid ""
"All of this let's users know that your xontrib is out there, ready to be "
"used. Of course, you're under no obligation to register your xontrib.  Users "
"will still be able to load your xontrib, as long as they have it installed."
msgstr ""

